  "2026-07-15T09:27:04.865Z",codex-root,"GitHub report coverage 2026-07-15: GH-569 reports a Complex Method in src/cli/bootstrap-args.ts. All-status exact search found no dedicated duplicate; this canonical complexity-baseline chore owns the report alongside the existing <=16 ratchet. The report is documented but remains open/unclaimed because PR #568 is actively limited to governance SDK review convergence."
  "2026-07-15T18:51:51.689Z",maintainer-agent,"GH-569 (CodeFactor Complex Method, src/cli/bootstrap-args.ts:94-169 parseBootstrapGlobalOptions) mapped here 2026-07-15 — file holds 2 grandfathered sonarjs/cognitive-complexity suppressions in eslint-suppressions.json. Close GH-569 when the bootstrap-args entries are burned down. No standalone item per baseline policy (GH-518/pm-2gvp precedent)."
  "2026-07-21T07:33:05.774Z",codex-root-20260721,"Progress evidence: decomposed both suppressed cli-bootstrap functions below cognitive complexity 16, pruned two suppressions, and ratcheted the repository maximum from 154 to 152. This advances but does not complete the broader 76-suppression burn-down item."
  "2026-07-21T07:39:44.598Z",codex-root-20260721,"Corrective evidence: the linked repo-wide ESLint run caught a new merge-dispatch cognitive score of 17 introduced in this branch. Refactored it immediately into explicit audited subcommand helpers; rerun passed with zero warnings and no suppression added."
  "2026-07-21T10:13:37.287Z",codex-root-20260721,"Hosted static-gate investigation: pnpm lint:eslint:prune against the exact branch head reports Already up to date, suppression count remains exactly 152, and pnpm lint:eslint passes locally. No artificial suppression or budget mutation made; the next hosted head reruns the gate."
  "2026-07-21T10:15:34.942Z",codex-root-20260721,"Exact prune result: stale sonarjs/cognitive-complexity entry for scripts/smoke-cleanup.mjs removed; suppression budget lowered in both package.json and static-quality-gate.mts from 152 to 151."
  "2026-07-21T10:19:07.769Z",codex-root-20260721,"Acceptance correction: linked release-automation contract caught its stale literal 152 after the ratchet; updated it to 151 so package script, gate constant, suppression inventory, and integration contract remain exact."
  "2026-07-21T10:25:06.160Z",codex-root-20260721,Full coverage preflight exposed the second stale 152 literal in release-readiness packaging parity. Updated to 151; all other 6052 tests passed in that run.
  "2026-07-21T10:29:28.720Z",codex-root-20260721,"Exact final-head proof: the 151 suppression ratchet, both package-script parity contracts, full ESLint, static quality, and all 6053 tests pass at 100/100/100/100 coverage. Broader suppression burn-down remains open."
  "2026-07-25T06:31:40.103Z","harness:claude-code","GitHub issues #569 (bootstrap-args.ts) and #583 (cli-bootstrap.ts) are CodeFactor Complex Method findings against grandfathered cognitive-complexity suppressions in eslint-suppressions.json, not new regressions. Both mapped to this burn-down on 2026-07-25 with comments on the issues; they close when the burn-down reaches those methods. No per-method items filed."
  "2026-07-30T09:54:49.182Z","harness:codex","GitHub intake 2026-07-30: GH-820 reports current corpus-shape method complexity. This canonical complexity burn-down owns the report and will actively decompose the method without adding or raising suppressions. https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/820"
  "2026-07-30T10:27:27.055Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: corpus measurement add() delegates reused mismatch and edge-count primitives, removes branch-heavy loops, and obsolete complexity suppressions were pruned; static CodeFactor-parity gate passes."
  "2026-07-30T11:24:17.779Z","harness:codex","Delivery boundary: this tranche reduced runtime/output/corpus-shape complexity, split action aliases into a focused module, pruned one suppression, and lowered the mandatory ESLint suppression ceiling from 130 to 129. The repo-wide complexity burn-down remains open."
  "2026-07-30T11:30:58.844Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/829 reviews cohesive SDK context budgets, universal row contracts, bounded graph/health diagnostics, quality ratchets, and exact-head commit e53544cd1."
  "2026-07-30T11:54:24.653Z","harness:codex","Review correction: extension active-command context tests now mutate args/options/global snapshots and prove a second read is unchanged; CI doc links and generated error contracts are current."
  "2026-07-30T11:54:34.409Z","harness:codex","Evidence clarification: e53544cd1 identifies the implementation commit. Exact-head review and merge proof is maintained on PR #829 because every append-only PM evidence mutation necessarily creates a newer Git head."
  "2026-08-04T09:18:08.088Z","harness:codex","Fresh suppression census 2026-08-04: eslint-suppressions.json contains 114 counted suppressions across 70 keyed files; source and tests also contain 383 c8 ignore pragmas, 5 eslint-disable directives, and 18 TypeScript suppression directives. These are distinct populations and must be ratcheted separately; literal coverage and the current static gate pass do not make the maintenance debt disappear."
  "2026-08-11T14:18:51.174Z","harness:claude-code","Ownership recorded 2026-08-11: open CodeFactor issues GH-569 (src/cli/bootstrap-args.ts:94-169) and GH-583 (src/sdk/cli-bootstrap.ts:94-171), both Complex Method, are members of this item's declared suppression population rather than separate items. Both GitHub issues now carry the canonical pm-link comment. Note the pairing - the two flagged ranges are near-identical line spans in two files that mirror each other, which is the bootstrap-args duplication this burndown will have to resolve structurally rather than by lowering complexity in each copy."
  "2026-08-28T02:09:54.943Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-28: exact-head PR #1133 hosted Gates (static) reports src/sdk/annotations.ts renderAnnotationResult cyclomatic complexity 17 against the mandatory ceiling 16. All-status duplicate searches for the exact function, hosted gate, and annotation result found no dedicated active item; reusing this canonical complexity-burn-down lineage. Scope is a behavior-preserving decomposition with no suppression or threshold change, focused regression proof, full static/coverage gates, and a fresh exact-head bot review cycle."
  "2026-08-28T02:14:39.226Z","harness:codex","Linked-test context correction: the legacy pnpm lint:codefactor entry defaulted to schema-only PM context, so repository-static-quality saw an empty tracker and correctly failed its defect-evidence assertion even though a direct source-tracker run passed. Replaced that entry with identical command semantics plus pm_context_mode=tracker; no gate, evidence rule, or threshold was weakened."
  "2026-08-28T02:19:51.886Z","harness:codex","Linked-test timeout calibration: tracker-context execution proved every repository assurance assertion, including defect evidence, then reached the legacy 300-second ceiling during downstream static gates. Raised only this linked command's execution allowance to 600 seconds; the command and every quality threshold remain unchanged."
  "2026-08-28T02:32:12.585Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: renderAnnotationResult is decomposed without suppressions or ceiling changes. pnpm exec eslint src/sdk/annotations.ts --max-warnings=0 --no-cache passed; focused annotation suite passed 3 files / 91 tests; repo-wide ESLint passed; tracker-context pnpm lint:codefactor passed all assurance and downstream static gates in 327454 ms; full coverage passed 585 files / 8076 tests at statements 59938/59938, branches 45128/45128, functions 12466/12466, lines 57719/57719. The earlier schema-context assertion failure and 300-second timeout remain immutable diagnostic receipts and are superseded by the corrected linked-test metadata and passing run."
  "2026-08-28T06:38:32.272Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review evidence: structured passing receipts now exist for no-cache annotation ESLint, the focused 3-file/91-test annotation suite, repository-wide ESLint, and full coverage. The terminal coverage receipt passed 8,083 tests across 585 files at statements 59,952/59,952, branches 45,139/45,139, functions 12,469/12,469, and lines 57,732/57,732. The broader suppression burn-down remains open."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T07:13:56.788Z","harness:claude-code","Complexity-suppression composition measured 2026-07-25 for the burn-down ledger. eslint-suppressions.json totals exactly 146 suppressions, at the hard MAX_ESLINT_SUPPRESSIONS = 146 budget in scripts/release/static-quality-gate.mts — zero headroom, so any new suppression fails the gate. Breakdown by rule: sonarjs/cognitive-complexity 52, complexity 38 (90 of 146, 62%, are the twin complexity gates this item owns), @typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars 22, no-useless-assignment 18, preserve-caught-error 16. Zero inline eslint-disable comments and zero broad disables (both budgets are 0 and both hold), and zero TODO/FIXME/HACK markers exist anywhere in src — the suppression file is the only debt ledger, which is the right shape; the ledger is simply full."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T02:32:12.127Z","harness:codex",Exact-head quality parity must include a no-cache ESLint run after the final source mutation. Repository-wide PM-aware static commands also need pm_context_mode=tracker and a timeout calibrated to the full governed gate; schema-only context can create a legitimate fail-closed defect-evidence result that is not a source-quality failure.
